# G036 — Fetch Current Weather

*v2. See `fetch-weather.md` for prose: first live external fact,
HTTP as FTP generalised with URLs + JSON, API key as shared secret,
unit conversion as frame translation, freshness as first-class
concern.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Weather-Aware Operations

[weather-check @cities
    IN ORDER TO
        fetch current weather for several cities concurrently
        validate that each snapshot is fresh enough to act on
        and only surface stale reports as resistance rather than silent

    concurrent
        @reports <- @cities mapped concurrently to
                     [weather[fetch {city: @c:name,
                                      country: @c:country}]]
    join

    @reports
        where every report:age-minutes is less than 15
            -> [compose[comparison {reports: @reports}]]
        otherwise
            -> #stale-weather {reports: @reports where age too large}
               (stale weather is worse than bad weather;
                at least bad weather is true)
]

---

## Verb Surface

[weather
    fetch           {city, country}          ;; -> Report | fetch-error
    compare         {reports}                 ;; -> Comparison
    convert-temp    {kelvin, to-unit}         ;; "C" | "F" | "K"
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: store canonical `where` consumer picks the frame

[weather[fetch {city: @c, country: @co}]
    IN ORDER TO
        return temperatures in Kelvin (the API's canonical frame)
        and let every consumer convert into their preferred frame on demand
        so no unit is baked into the report itself

    HTTP GET api/weather?q=@c,@co with api-key
        where status is 200
            -> parse JSON response
            -> build Report with temp-kelvin (not F, not C)
            -> record fetched-at-ms for age tracking
        where status is 401 -> #api-key-rejected
        where status is 429 -> #rate-limited
        where timeout        -> #unreachable
]

Same normalise-to-base pattern G010 introduced: the API is the
authority, Kelvin is the base unit, every consumer gets a frame-
translated view via `convert-temp`.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: freshness as a `where` the caller enforces

[@report
    where age-minutes is less than @freshness-budget
        -> use in choreography
    otherwise
        -> #stale (re-fetch or proceed with known-stale marker)
]

The resolver does not silently re-fetch. Callers declare the
freshness budget; the choreography either uses a fresh report or
explicitly acknowledges a stale one. Same discipline G044's session
expiry uses.

---

## Demo

[demo
    concurrent
        @jax    <- [weather[fetch {city: "Jacksonville", country: "US"}]]
    |
        @london <- [weather[fetch {city: "London",       country: "GB"}]]
    |
        @tokyo  <- [weather[fetch {city: "Tokyo",        country: "JP"}]]
    join

    -> [weather[compare {reports: [@jax, @london, @tokyo]}]]
    ;; -> {warmest: tokyo, coldest: london, wettest: london, ...}

    -> [weather[convert-temp {kelvin: @jax:temp-kelvin, to-unit: "F"}]]
    ;; -> e.g. 78.3
]
